  "title": "Pellet guns and crowd control: A mix of denial and allegations",
  "summary": "Pellet guns, which were once used as non-lethal crowd-control measures, have been recalled by the government after reports of civilian injuries during protests in Punjab. However, the use of such weapons has been contested, with police denying their involvement in the incidents.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Pellet guns were last reported in the 2024 farmers protest in Khanuari and Shambhu barriers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Farmers claimed some injuries were caused by pellet guns, though police denied their use.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The first known case of security forces using pellet guns in Delhi involved Shaikh Irshad Mansoori, but police claimed the use was illegal.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
